            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Overall in support of this, just want to make sure we're not excluding certain contributions for the sake of something that (to my understanding) LF doesn't recommend."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I've tried to incorporate your feedback @ed@tanous.net.  Please take a look."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "LGTM"
                },
                {
                    "file": "CONTRIBUTING.md",
                    "line": 490,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Remove the \"should not\"\n\nJust keep the \"should\". Maybe even go to \"shall\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "CONTRIBUTING.md",
                    "line": 490,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "The suggestion you are making is that we should have large copyright blocks?  ie a copy of the Apache license in each file?  That\u2019s exactly the opposite of what I\u2019m aiming for here. We don\u2019t need Apache copied in each file; we just reference SPDX."
                },
                {
                    "file": "CONTRIBUTING.md",
                    "line": 490,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "No, copyright blocks can go.  I meant to remove the highlighted block.\n\n\"Contributions to OpenBMC shall leverage [SPDX file tags][spdx] for declaring copyrights.\"\n\nNo need to mention what we shouldn't do, at least in the first sentence.  Lets just keep this about what we \"should\" do and not give people ideas.\n\nWe could also add \"Other mechanisms of denoting copyright require Technical oversight forum approval\", but I'm not sure even that is needed."
                },
                {
                    "file": "CONTRIBUTING.md",
                    "line": 490,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "CONTRIBUTING.md",
                    "line": 493,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "The \"rather\" part isn't really in line what what LF says.\n\nIt allows for both if it's required.\n\n\"Please note that it is not wrong, and it is acceptable, if a contributor wishes to keep their own copyright notices on their contributions.\"\n\nAnd I think that if we pull code from anywhere else that already has a copyright, we need to retain that, so this would require all code to be \"new\" code.    I personally don't care that much, but there's companies where they make this requirement (arbitrarily) and I don't think that's a reason to disallow a contribution.  With that said, if we have something where LF says \"no company copyrights\" then that's easy to point to an authority and not be inventing our own policy here.\n\n\nI think this doc should express a requirement for Copyright OpenBMC authors, and a preference for not including the per-company names, without explicitly disallowing it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "CONTRIBUTING.md",
                    "line": 493,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "See the \u201cWhy not list every copyright holder?\u201d section. We are allowed, per LF, to ask them not be added. They give a number of rationales but the two most important to me, as a maintainer, is:\n\n> * Trying to keep notices up to date, or to correct notices that have become inaccurate, increases the burden on developers without tangible benefit.\n> * Developers and maintainers often do not want to have to worry about e.g. whether a minor contribution (such as a typo fix) means that a new copyright notice should be added.\n\nI\u2019m ok adding something about \u201ccode copied from elsewhere\u201d but we should be clear that \u201ccopied from elsewhere\u201d means somewhere in open source and not a \u201cinternal codebase we are contributing to the project\u201d."
                },
                {
                    "file": "CONTRIBUTING.md",
                    "line": 493,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> means somewhere in open source and not a \u201cinternal codebase we are contributing to the project\u201d.\n\nAgreed, where I worry about this is if someone finds code in someones public fork, and finds it useful enough they want to contribute it back to the project.  If we have this rule, and the code has a copyright on it, they can't contribute it.\n\nFor original contributions or contributions where the original author is involved in the contribution, I agree, \"OpenBMC Authors\" should suffice and we should voice that preference here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "CONTRIBUTING.md",
                    "line": 493,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                }
            ],
