                    },
                    "message": "Any specific reason for adding cpp hint here . i think it is applicable for all types of source codes right?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "CONTRIBUTING.md",
                    "line": 498,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> Any specific reason for adding cpp hint here \n\nA code block needs a source language otherwise the linter starts to cry.\n\nDo you think we should add examples for other languages like python?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "CONTRIBUTING.md",
                    "line": 498,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                        "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ojayanth"
                    },
                    "message": "To keep Markdown linters happy, use text instead of cpp for SPDX tag code blocks may be another option."
                },
                {
                    "file": "CONTRIBUTING.md",
                    "line": 498,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "c++ is currently the most widely used and the sample is c++ comment syntax. I\u2019d expect most people to know how to convert on their own to their preferred language. Using cpp identifier allows syntax highlighting. \n\nI\u2019m going to leave this."
                }
            ],
